      "unit_index": 1,
      "source_text": "古歌：“蜉蝣生即死，似有亦如无。",
      "en": [
        {
          "t": "An old poem says: \"The mayfly is born and at once dies, seeming to exist and yet as if it does not.",
          "g": "predicate"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "paragraph_id": "genji-modern-p05423",
      "unit_index": 2,
      "source_text": "世事皆如此，莫谈荣与枯。”",
      "en": [
        {
          "t": "All worldly things are like this; do not speak of flourishing or withering.\"",
          "g": "predicate"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "paragraph_id": "genji-modern-p05423",
      "unit_index": 3,
      "source_text": "见《后撰集》。",
      "en": [
        {
          "t": "It appears in the Gosenshu.",
          "g": "predicate"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
